// The combine notation: `-@name(...)`, no space between the list marker
// and `@`. Parses `@name(...)` through the exact same element-parsing
// path a standalone, top-level `@name(...)` would -- same `Element`
// shape, no naming constraint, no second grammar. Position (list item)
// and naming (what kind of thing it is) are orthogonal.

// Bare combine item, no groups at all.
-@task()

// `[content]`, a bare trailing connect, and a named connect, same as a
// standalone element's own groups.
-@task()[content]:rule(allow:list(card))
-@task():(x: 1){y: 2}

// Ordered list marker, same combine support.
-.@task()

// A nested list under a combine item is that item's own `sublist`,
// same as a plain bare item's.
-@task() a
  - b
